WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.230
Grindavík, on Iceland's
Reykjanes Peninsula,

2
00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.710
where the Mid-Atlantic
Ridge rises above sea level.

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.970
On 10 November 2023, a blade
of magma cut beneath the town.

4
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.510
About 3,700 people were
evacuated that same day.

5
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.290
Half the town dropped more than a metre.

6
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:21.370
Then eruptions began.

7
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:26.170
In January 2024, earth barriers
turned the main lava flow west.

8
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.530
But a second fissure opened outside them,

9
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.990
at the edge of town.

10
00:00:30.040 --> 00:00:32.750
So how has the hazard reshaped the town?

11
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.850
Did everyone stay and rebuild?

12
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.510
In this mission, you'll explain the physical
hazards of a plate boundary on land.

13
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.610
Then you'll analyse the town's economic,
social and political character,

14
00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.050
and how each reflects the risk.

15
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.050
Your mission: explain how the
hazard has reshaped Grindavík.
